After fixing syntax errors in test_table_url everything worked. There are no issues with links in tables at all.

 output$test_table_url <- renderText( {
    str <- "<table border = 1>"

    for (i in 1:input$n) {

      str <- paste0(str, "<tr>")
      str <- paste0(str, "<td>", "<a href='http://google.com'>google</a>", "</td></tr>")
    }
    str
  })

That said, I still prefer generating tags for tables myself for more flexibility with applying CSS like centering text in columns or cell conditional formatting based on content. Also there are interactive and sortable tables like googleVis and Foo Tables <https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/shiny-discuss/_pOT2AkKF4Q>. The latter never worked for me and ones from google do not display correctly in Chrome (what an irony).

